WEBVTT

00:03.550 --> 00:06.120
What is the reason of my birth?

00:06.300 --> 00:10.230
Reason of my life, question of man.

00:10.240 --> 00:13.830
What he is?

00:14.020 --> 00:18.410
What he wants?

00:22.080 --> 00:29.490
Ima kimi ni mienai chikara ga osoi.
Now you are being troubled by an unseen power.

00:29.490 --> 00:34.560
Utsumuite namida kakushiteta.
You hang your head and hide your tears.

00:36.840 --> 00:43.820
Dou sureba ii ka? Sore sae wakarazu ni!
What should be done? That's unknown!

00:44.240 --> 00:51.690
Asphalt ni saku hana ni yuuki kanjita...
Blooming in the asphalt is a flower of courage...

00:53.490 --> 00:56.980
Itsumo kimi no soba ni iru yo.
We'll always be by your side.

00:57.200 --> 01:00.490
Da kara mou hitori ja nai.
So you're not alone anymore.

01:00.840 --> 01:04.340
Kimi ga michi ni mayou toki wa...
When you lose your way...

01:04.560 --> 01:07.920
Boku ga saki o aruku yo.
I'll walk ahead and lead you.

01:08.220 --> 01:11.750
Tooi sora koete...
Crossing to the far away sky...

01:11.950 --> 01:15.300
Bokura wa tobitatsu!
We're flying!

01:15.620 --> 01:19.140
Kitto soko ni aru...
It'll definitely be there...

01:19.140 --> 01:24.050
Sore ga kimi no yume
Your dream...

01:30.770 --> 01:35.390
Venus Robot

01:41.080 --> 01:43.410
All right, pull in the net!

01:45.020 --> 01:47.310
It's a big haul!
A big haul!

01:47.650 --> 01:51.160
Keep pulling!
Take the hook off!

01:57.230 --> 01:58.920
What the--?

02:02.800 --> 02:05.620
Something weird got in the net.

02:14.040 --> 02:18.280
Captain?

02:32.500 --> 02:35.600
Atom, this is a Venus Robot.

02:35.640 --> 02:37.330
Venus Robot?

02:37.670 --> 02:41.070
Right. I believe we have
some old footage.

02:41.640 --> 02:44.370
This kind of robot was
manufactured 20 years ago.

02:44.400 --> 02:47.770
That was when space exploration
was flourishing.

02:48.210 --> 02:51.410
The humans had already succeeded
in developing the moon and Mars...

02:51.440 --> 02:55.350
...and we were taking on an even more
challenging task of developing Venus.

02:55.720 --> 02:58.700
But in the extreme heat
and high pressure on Venus...

02:58.790 --> 03:02.640
...ordinary robots were
immediately incapacitated.

03:03.040 --> 03:05.490
That's why they had to develop
these Venus Robots...

03:05.600 --> 03:10.760
...with an extremely strong body
and powerful freezing capability.

03:20.930 --> 03:23.560
Unbelievable! It's freezing
in just a matter of seconds!

03:23.610 --> 03:28.090
It was a simulated image.
The experiment on Earth was successful

03:28.090 --> 03:31.530
...and people had high expectations
for Venus Robots.

03:31.570 --> 03:35.710
However, they were never
sent to Venus.

03:36.330 --> 03:37.870
Why was that?

03:37.910 --> 03:41.160
The cruising range of robots
improved dramatically...

03:41.200 --> 03:46.400
and the main focus of space exploration
shifted to the satellite clusters of Jupiter.

03:47.000 --> 03:50.180
Venus Robots with such powerful
freezing capabilities...

03:50.210 --> 03:53.150
...were considered dangerous.

03:53.340 --> 03:56.670
Therefore, I heard they had been
completely incapacitated...

03:56.700 --> 03:59.760
...and discarded deep in the sea.

03:59.850 --> 04:04.340
So Venus Robots couldn't be of
any service to the humans at all.

04:04.420 --> 04:05.910
Even so, it's strange.

04:05.930 --> 04:10.270
This robot appears to have
been active until quite recently.

04:10.390 --> 04:13.260
We may need to investigate
more thoroughly.

04:13.280 --> 04:15.410
Let's get ready for
a closer examination.

04:15.500 --> 04:17.510
Who are you?

04:17.510 --> 04:18.550
What?

04:18.590 --> 04:22.120
Are you our captain?

04:22.230 --> 04:23.350
Captain?

04:24.640 --> 04:26.000
Dr. Ochanomizu

04:26.030 --> 04:29.980
Please let me investigate the area
in the ocean where this Venus Robot was found.

04:30.560 --> 04:34.310
That's probably necessary.
We're counting on you, Atom.

04:35.790 --> 04:37.700
I believe this is the area in question.

04:37.790 --> 04:38.920
This is it!

04:51.670 --> 04:53.900
It's too dark to see anything.

05:21.030 --> 05:22.960
I wonder what that is.

05:23.970 --> 05:27.530
It looks just like a city of humans
on the land.

05:44.350 --> 05:48.510
Awesome!
Did you guys build all these?

05:48.550 --> 05:50.240
Who are you?

05:50.260 --> 05:55.130
I'm Atom. Just like you,
I'm a robot created by humans.

05:55.200 --> 05:57.520
Humans? That's not true.

05:57.550 --> 06:00.280
It was the captain who created us.

06:00.370 --> 06:03.310
Captain? Who in the world
is the captain?

06:03.410 --> 06:06.170
Come with me.
I'll let you see him.

06:07.340 --> 06:11.040
Our fellow robot headed
for the surface of the sea.

06:11.410 --> 06:13.410
And he has not returned yet.

06:13.610 --> 06:15.410
He was damaged.

06:15.690 --> 06:17.030
Damaged?

06:17.650 --> 06:22.040
He was caught in an electromagnetic net on
a fishing trawler damaging his electronic brain.

06:22.130 --> 06:27.860
I told him he should wait and that
the captain would certainly show up.

06:29.400 --> 06:32.710
Look. This is our captain.

06:33.900 --> 06:39.500
We were created by the captain.
That's why we're waiting for him.

06:39.710 --> 06:44.380
We're waiting for the day he will appear
in front of us and give us orders.

06:44.410 --> 06:45.630
Orders?

06:45.720 --> 06:49.620
We have long forgotten...
the reason why we were created.

06:49.720 --> 06:51.580
Captain, huh?

06:51.750 --> 06:56.230
We want to know why we were created
and to fulfill our original purpose.

06:56.260 --> 06:56.950
What?

06:57.750 --> 06:59.660
But you guys are--

06:59.660 --> 07:00.810
Atom...

07:00.890 --> 07:03.670
...what purpose were you
created to serve?

07:03.700 --> 07:06.640
I was created to become
a friend to humans.

07:06.640 --> 07:08.740
A friend?

07:11.040 --> 07:15.060
Atom, if you happen
to see our captain...

07:15.610 --> 07:17.740
...please tell him that
we are waiting for him.

07:17.990 --> 07:19.290
Sure.

07:21.050 --> 07:25.250
They don't know that they
were abandoned by the humans.

07:25.290 --> 07:27.710
I need to let Dr. Ochanomizu
know this right away!

07:29.430 --> 07:31.370
Excellent.

07:31.760 --> 07:36.890
Venus Robots have created
a world of their own...

07:37.260 --> 07:40.410
...beyond the wildest imagination
of humans. And for20 years...

07:40.410 --> 07:43.400
...they have been patiently waiting for
orders from the captain, their creator.

07:43.510 --> 07:49.050
I will take advantage of you all
to realize the world of my dreams.

07:52.380 --> 07:54.360
My dear robots!

07:56.180 --> 07:59.100
I'm your captain.

08:00.890 --> 08:05.710
The time has come to tell you the
true reason why you were created.

08:08.350 --> 08:09.830
Captain!

08:13.220 --> 08:14.510
Unbelievable!

08:14.880 --> 08:19.640
Venus Robots continued to evolve on their
own and continue to duplicate themselves...

08:19.760 --> 08:24.140
...in order to execute the trace
of orders left in their brains.

08:24.450 --> 08:28.370
Dr. Ochanomizu, what would become
of the Venus Robots?

08:28.380 --> 08:30.120
I have no idea.

08:30.210 --> 08:32.790
But we can't leave them
as they are now.

08:32.790 --> 08:33.590
What?

08:33.590 --> 08:38.220
They possess a special capability to freeze
anything in a matter of seconds.

08:38.330 --> 08:41.980
If they land on our city,
it will be disaster.

08:47.340 --> 08:50.030
You mean, you will destroy them?

08:50.040 --> 08:52.920
Of course I'd rather not,
if I could avoid it.

08:53.080 --> 08:55.280
But the worst-case scenario is--

08:55.280 --> 08:56.610
Oh, no!

09:17.130 --> 09:18.390
What--? What are those?

09:18.480 --> 09:20.250
A whole bunch of monsters!

09:33.120 --> 09:34.770
What in the world is happening?

09:34.820 --> 09:35.930
What's the latest?

09:35.930 --> 09:39.090
Approximately 20,000 robots
have landed from various places.

09:39.270 --> 09:41.270
Twenty thousand?

09:41.360 --> 09:42.950
What are they?
What's going on?

09:47.060 --> 09:51.470
They are eliminating all obstacles
and marching through Metro City.

09:52.120 --> 09:54.360
Why did they come onto land?

09:54.700 --> 09:56.970
Where in the world are they heading?

10:03.160 --> 10:06.010
Here is the projected course
and their final destination!

10:07.850 --> 10:09.370
The Ministry of Science!

10:09.420 --> 10:13.250
You mean the Venus Robots
are heading for our office?

10:13.300 --> 10:15.180
But why?

10:20.660 --> 10:21.730
Atom,

10:21.800 --> 10:24.170
even you can't stop them.

10:24.230 --> 10:26.840
The order I gave them ...

10:26.870 --> 10:28.270
is absolute.

10:33.010 --> 10:38.050
Listen up. Do not let those robots
go beyond this point!

10:39.040 --> 10:40.440
Aim!

10:43.110 --> 10:43.750
Fire--!

10:43.750 --> 10:45.080
Hold it!

10:45.420 --> 10:49.460
Their body is full of extremely
powerful freezing gas.

10:49.530 --> 10:51.250
You can't use firearms on them!

10:51.250 --> 10:52.350
What?

10:52.430 --> 10:56.800
I'll try to talk to them.
You should all evacuate for your safety.

10:59.810 --> 11:01.490
Please, wait!

11:01.570 --> 11:02.700
Atom.

11:02.710 --> 11:05.780
Why did you decide
to come out of the water?

11:06.040 --> 11:10.610
We met our captain...
and received an order.

11:10.680 --> 11:11.390
What?

11:11.410 --> 11:14.680
There is only one reason
why we were created.

11:14.750 --> 11:17.530
It is to create a new world.

11:17.650 --> 11:21.170
When we complete our mission,
we'll become happy.

11:21.220 --> 11:24.860
A new world?
What do they mean by that?

11:26.000 --> 11:29.400
We're going to a certain place
to take off our cap.

11:29.530 --> 11:31.760
That's the order from our captain.

11:31.800 --> 11:33.490
What is your cap?

11:33.500 --> 11:34.590
Don't tell me!

11:38.410 --> 11:39.430
Oh, no!

11:39.740 --> 11:42.620
It's the switch to discharge
the super freezing gas!

11:42.650 --> 11:44.820
You were all deceived!

11:44.820 --> 11:46.280
Deceived?

11:46.280 --> 11:48.880
There is no way anyone would
have given you an order!

11:50.320 --> 11:54.830
If you take off your caps this city will
freeze in just a matter of seconds!

11:54.860 --> 11:59.260
To the humans you are
very dangerous robots.

11:59.790 --> 12:00.890
Move over!

12:00.990 --> 12:03.960
It was the captain who created us!

12:05.130 --> 12:07.830
The captain's order is absolute!

12:08.540 --> 12:11.010
What's the current status
of the Venus Robots?

12:11.040 --> 12:13.960
Currently, they are passing
through Area D.

12:13.980 --> 12:17.240
In approximately 20 minutes they are
estimated to reach the Ministry of Science.

12:17.580 --> 12:20.310
We should evacuate for safety.

12:21.220 --> 12:26.630
Make an announcement.
Instruct all employees to evacuate
the Ministry building in five minutes.

12:26.660 --> 12:28.050
But--

12:28.160 --> 12:29.950
Go on! Hurry up, now!

12:39.030 --> 12:41.150
There's nothing we can do!

12:44.200 --> 12:45.280
No! Stop!

12:45.430 --> 12:47.410
Everyone, don't go!

12:47.640 --> 12:50.940
Dr. Ochanomizu, as your secretary,
I will stay here too.

12:51.010 --> 12:54.560
I can handle processing
important data by myself.

12:54.610 --> 12:56.510
Yuko, you should evacuate.

12:56.520 --> 12:57.510
But--

12:57.590 --> 12:59.020
Don't worry.

12:59.090 --> 13:02.300
As soon as I finish processing
the data, I will evacuate too.

13:02.370 --> 13:07.850
Besides, I believe that Atom will
be able to stop those Venus Robots.

13:09.700 --> 13:10.780
Doctor....

13:12.400 --> 13:16.240
Please, stop!
Your captain no longer exists!

13:16.240 --> 13:19.970
Our captain does exist.
He's waiting for us over there.

13:19.970 --> 13:20.780
What?

13:24.080 --> 13:26.470
Atom, hang in there!

13:26.550 --> 13:28.160
Huh? What is it?

13:28.390 --> 13:33.250
What a foolish man.
Do you really think you can stop them?

13:33.360 --> 13:36.140
That voice! Dr. Tenma?

13:36.530 --> 13:41.360
Hurry up and leave before
you get frozen.

13:41.670 --> 13:44.810
So you tricked the Venus Robots!

13:45.970 --> 13:49.790
I simply ordered them to pursue
an original mission.

13:49.830 --> 13:51.300
What did you say?

13:51.330 --> 13:54.840
They were created for the purpose
of freezing anything and everything.

13:54.840 --> 13:58.330
And you took advantage of that
as a tool for revenge!

13:58.380 --> 14:01.900
Dr. Tenma, you're
unbelievably egotistical!

14:01.930 --> 14:06.880
As soon as Venus Robots became useless
humans discarded them in the deep sea.

14:06.920 --> 14:10.650
Aren't humans even more egotistical?

14:14.500 --> 14:17.600
They survived on their own will.

14:17.970 --> 14:20.990
Finally, the robots started to evolve.

14:21.600 --> 14:26.140
Freed from human control,
they will eventually subdue humans.

14:26.600 --> 14:28.260
Are you serious?

14:28.590 --> 14:32.720
This is a grandiose ceremony
to declare the independence of robots.

14:32.820 --> 14:36.920
They will use their sealed powers to
let humans know how foolish they are.

14:36.970 --> 14:40.910
The Ministry of Science is the most
appropriate location for that to happen.

14:42.260 --> 14:46.460
Certainly, the humans acted selfishly
towards the Venus Robots!

14:46.500 --> 14:50.950
But to recall them and use them
for destruction is evil.

14:50.950 --> 14:56.000
I'm leading those robots
into the future. I'm their god!

15:00.950 --> 15:01.980
What's that?

15:04.810 --> 15:06.420
My dear robots...

15:06.650 --> 15:10.420
...take off your caps immediately
to create the new age!

15:10.590 --> 15:13.770
Just as we thought.
The captain was waiting for us here.

15:14.120 --> 15:17.440
Wake up! He's not your captain!

15:17.520 --> 15:19.930
You are all being deceived!

15:35.750 --> 15:38.050
Finally, the time has come!

15:38.250 --> 15:40.840
The time to fulfill our mission!

15:44.450 --> 15:45.580
Don't!

15:52.560 --> 15:55.700
I won't let you become
a terrifying robot!

15:56.530 --> 15:57.580
Atom!

15:57.620 --> 15:58.540
You idiot!

15:58.590 --> 16:00.340
You'll be blown to pieces!

16:07.570 --> 16:08.740
Got it!

16:23.060 --> 16:24.780
Atom!

16:33.640 --> 16:34.760
Atom!

16:35.300 --> 16:37.650
Are you all right? Atom!

16:43.180 --> 16:47.390
Now you see, right?
You are freeze robots.

16:47.450 --> 16:51.300
You were created to be useful
to humans.

16:51.390 --> 16:56.430
But if you take off your caps here...
this city of people will freeze.

16:56.490 --> 16:59.710
And you will destroy
their happiness.

17:02.730 --> 17:05.020
Then why were we created?

17:05.090 --> 17:07.630
Why did the captain give us
such an order?

17:07.680 --> 17:08.580
That's because--

17:08.580 --> 17:10.250
Don't be confused.

17:10.740 --> 17:13.790
Only when you freeze everything...

17:13.940 --> 17:18.280
and fulfill your original mission...
can you become happy.

17:18.630 --> 17:22.150
To freeze everything
is our happiness?

17:22.220 --> 17:26.400
That's right.
And that is my wish, your captain.

17:26.530 --> 17:31.290
You're wrong!
The true captain would not wish such a thing!

17:34.000 --> 17:36.400
Wait! You're all free!

17:37.040 --> 17:40.550
You have the power to choose
your own future.

17:40.940 --> 17:42.220
I feel so weak.

17:42.220 --> 17:43.250
Atom!

17:45.140 --> 17:49.790
I know! All I need to do is show the
true record of the past to the Venus Robots.

17:59.330 --> 18:02.070
Don't! It's useless to resist.

18:02.240 --> 18:03.520
Is it really?

18:06.900 --> 18:09.630
Yuko, why did you come back?

18:09.720 --> 18:12.550
I believe in Atom too.

18:18.890 --> 18:22.270
This is our last hope. Please! Work!

18:46.740 --> 18:49.130
Finally the experiment was successful.

18:49.170 --> 18:52.750
You're all taking off shortly
to outer space...

18:52.770 --> 18:56.090
...in order to create a beautiful new
world on Venus...

18:57.300 --> 19:00.050
...for the future of humans.

19:00.080 --> 19:01.880
We understand, captain.

19:01.950 --> 19:04.150
For the happiness of the humans!

19:04.250 --> 19:06.450
For the happiness of the humans!

19:07.120 --> 19:10.570
That lady is the captain
of the Venus Robots?

19:10.930 --> 19:12.080
Captain.

19:17.000 --> 19:18.800
My dear captain...

19:18.800 --> 19:22.770
...we're now leaving to go realize
the dreams of the humans.

19:22.870 --> 19:25.430
Very well. Go do your best.

19:32.010 --> 19:36.070
So you guarantee that their system
will be completely shut down?

19:36.090 --> 19:39.920
Before they reach the sea bottom,
all their memories will be erased...

19:39.920 --> 19:42.260
...and they will be
completely incapacitated.

19:42.260 --> 19:47.160
Very good. This is the end of recording.
The disposal of this nuisance is complete.

19:47.460 --> 19:50.560
Goodbye, my boys.

19:51.330 --> 19:53.390
Captain Helen.

19:53.710 --> 19:55.860
Do you think they understood?

19:56.410 --> 19:57.440
What's that?

19:57.840 --> 20:00.570
What's the matter?
Why aren't you moving?

20:00.710 --> 20:01.940
Dr. Tenma!

20:02.000 --> 20:03.980
Don't be tricked by such a thing!

20:04.010 --> 20:07.040
Your captain is over here. It's me!

20:07.420 --> 20:10.080
No, you're not our captain.

20:10.080 --> 20:11.590
That's right. That's right.

20:11.650 --> 20:14.300
Everyone! So you understood!

20:15.420 --> 20:17.360
You meddled with my plan!

20:32.490 --> 20:33.500
Atom.

20:45.090 --> 20:49.040
Venus Robots saved
Dr. Ochanomizu and Atom!

21:00.540 --> 21:03.100
Thank you for saving us!

21:03.340 --> 21:05.880
We're the ones who
need to thank you.

21:05.940 --> 21:06.740
What?

21:06.780 --> 21:12.330
Atom we're going back to the sea.
That's where our city is.

21:12.350 --> 21:13.880
The city of freedom.

21:13.920 --> 21:15.020
You're right.

21:15.050 --> 21:19.420
We'll never come back to the land.
Goodbye, Atom.

21:19.860 --> 21:21.220
Goodbye!

21:22.110 --> 21:23.680
Goodbye!

21:32.770 --> 21:37.070
These were filmed by an unmanned
exploratory mechanism.

21:37.210 --> 21:40.810
Dr. Ochanomizu,
where have they gone?

21:40.830 --> 21:44.080
Probably somewhere
we'll never be able to see.

21:44.150 --> 21:47.270
Somewhere at the bottom
of the deepest sea.

22:01.100 --> 22:04.560
Atom, our friend.

22:12.100 --> 22:17.630
Naze... Naze... Kokoro ga...
Why... Why... is my heart...

22:18.030 --> 22:23.240
Itamu to namida ni naru?
Is filled with pain and tears?

22:23.620 --> 22:29.130
Naze... Naze... Namida ga...
Why... Why... Tears...

22:29.410 --> 22:34.710
Ochiru to Hitori ni naru.
They fall and I'm alone.

22:35.070 --> 22:40.350
Chiisa na hiza kakae...
I hold my tiny knees...

22:40.830 --> 22:48.990
Tooku wo mata miageru.
And look up and far away.

22:49.390 --> 22:52.270
Hiroi... Hiroi...
Vast... Vast...

22:52.480 --> 23:00.480
Kono sora yori motto hiroi hazu da!
It has to be more wide than these skies!

23:01.070 --> 23:03.480
Takai... Takai...
High... High...

23:03.910 --> 23:12.190
Ano kumo yori motto takai hazu da!
It has to be higher than those clouds!

23:12.490 --> 23:17.220
Kimi no kokoro mo...
Your heart is...

23:23.410 --> 23:25.680
The Robot Circus is lots of fun!

23:25.850 --> 23:30.560
But why would you pretend to be
a robot when you're a human?

23:30.670 --> 23:33.780
Next time :
Robot Circus.

23:33.780 --> 23:36.590
With your heart, catch the future!
